    "rarity": "rare",
    "edition": "remaster",
    "publication": "Pathfinder #202: Severed at the Root",
    "path": "packs/pf2e/equipment/clear-cutters-axe.json",
    "description": "<p>Wielded by wealthy Taldan knights against the Goroth Lodge, this +1 striking returning hatchet has an axe head resembling a roaring lion's head.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Activate—Slash and Burn</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">r</span> (manipulate)</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> You critically succeed at a Strike against a plant</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The weapon's etchings pulse with green energy, as it tears through bark, leaf, and wood. The clear cutter's axe deals an additional @Damage[1d10[persistent,fire]] damage to the plant.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Activate—Mow Down</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">2</span> (manipulate)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You hurl the axe horizontally, sending it flying through the air in a wild, whirling cyclone. The axe flies in a @Template[emanation|distance:30] around you, eliminating all non-magical undergrowth and any resulting difficult terrain, cover, and concealment in area. It attempts to counteract one magical effect that affects a plant in the area (counteract [[/r 1d20+20 #Counteract]]{+20}). Plant creatures in the area take @Damage[5d6[slashing]] damage (@Check[reflex|dc:25|basic] save). As the axe finishes its circuit, it returns to your hand.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "Wielded by wealthy Taldan knights against the Goroth Lodge, this +1 striking returning hatchet has an axe head resembling a roaring lion's head. Activate—Slash and Burn r (manipulate) Trigger You critically succeed at a Strike against a plant Effect The weapon's etchings pulse with green energy, as it tears through bark, leaf, and wood. The clear cutter's axe deals an additional @Damage[1d10[persistent,fire]] damage to the plant. Activate—Mow Down 2 (manipulate) Frequency once per day Effect You hurl the axe horizontally, sending it flying through the air in a wild, whirling cyclone. The axe flies in a @Template[emanation|distance:30] around you, eliminating all non-magical undergrowth and any resulting difficult terrain, cover, and concealment in area. It attempts to counteract one magical effect that affects a plant in the area (counteract [[/r 1d20+20 #Counteract]]{+20}). Plant creatures in the area take @Damage[5d6[slashing]] damage (@Check[reflex|dc:25|basic] save). As the axe finishes its circuit, it returns to your hand.",
