    "rarity": "common",
    "edition": "remaster",
    "publication": "Pathfinder Impossible Magic",
    "path": "packs/pf2e/equipment/hundred-moth-caress.json",
    "description": "<p>This +1 striking scythe's handles are made from a dull gray wood of bone-like consistency, and when you slice with it, a fluttering gust of hundreds of moths' wingbeats fills the air. If you're a devotee of Urgathoa, you can use this scythe as a divine locus, and with every Strike, it exudes a pallid cloud of powdery dust.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Pallid Reaping</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">f</span> (concentrate, manipulate, spellshape, void)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> You deal @Damage[1d10[void]] damage to yourself. This damage ignores all resistances and immunities, and you take it even if you would be healed by void effects. If your next action is to Strike with the scythe or to Cast a Spell with the disease or void trait, that Strike or spell deals additional void damage equal to the damage you took.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "This +1 striking scythe's handles are made from a dull gray wood of bone-like consistency, and when you slice with it, a fluttering gust of hundreds of moths' wingbeats fills the air. If you're a devotee of Urgathoa, you can use this scythe as a divine locus, and with every Strike, it exudes a pallid cloud of powdery dust. Activate—Pallid Reaping f (concentrate, manipulate, spellshape, void) Frequency once per round Effect You deal @Damage[1d10[void]] damage to yourself. This damage ignores all resistances and immunities, and you take it even if you would be healed by void effects. If your next action is to Strike with the scythe or to Cast a Spell with the disease or void trait, that Strike or spell deals additional void damage equal to the damage you took.",
