    "rarity": "uncommon",
    "edition": "legacy",
    "publication": "Pathfinder Book of the Dead",
    "path": "packs/pf2e/equipment/ladys-spiral.json",
    "description": "<p>This <em>+1 @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.Vitalizing] striking whip</em> has a single strip of anointed leather wrapped around its hilt in a spiral pattern. The handle of the whip ends in an oak spike that has been sanctified with ashes from Pharasma's Boneyard. If the spike is used to stake a vampire that's vulnerable to being staked, the vampire is immediately destroyed, without having to sever its head and anoint it with holy water. If the whip is buried with a creature, that creature can't rise as an undead as long as the whip remains by its side.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "This +1 Vitalizing striking whip has a single strip of anointed leather wrapped around its hilt in a spiral pattern. The handle of the whip ends in an oak spike that has been sanctified with ashes from Pharasma's Boneyard. If the spike is used to stake a vampire that's vulnerable to being staked, the vampire is immediately destroyed, without having to sever its head and anoint it with holy water. If the whip is buried with a creature, that creature can't rise as an undead as long as the whip remains by its side.",
