    "path": "packs/pf2e/equipment/monkeys-fist.json",
    "description": "<p>Also called a \"slungshot\", the monkey's fist is a short length of rope ending in a thick knot wrapped around a metal weight. You can tie the loose end of a monkey's fist to your wrist; if you are @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Disarm]{Disarmed}, the weapon remains secured to your wrist rather than falling to the ground, though you must use an Interact action to grip it before using it again. A monkey's fist is a martial melee weapon.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "Also called a \"slungshot\", the monkey's fist is a short length of rope ending in a thick knot wrapped around a metal weight. You can tie the loose end of a monkey's fist to your wrist; if you are Disarmed, the weapon remains secured to your wrist rather than falling to the ground, though you must use an Interact action to grip it before using it again. A monkey's fist is a martial melee weapon.",
