    "edition": "remaster",
    "publication": "Pathfinder Impossible Magic",
    "path": "packs/pf2e/equipment/ouroboros-flail-greater.json",
    "description": "<p>You can easily magically expand and contract the chain of this <em>+3 greater striking greater extending war flail</em>.</p><hr /><p><strong>Activate—Chained Grasp</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">r</span> (concentrate)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> You successfully Strike with the ouroboros flail as part of activating its extending rune</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The head of the flail wraps around the target of the triggering Strike and drags it in your direction. The target must succeed at a @Check[fortitude|dc:37] save or be pulled adjacent to you. A creature pulled to you is then @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Grabbed] by the flail until the end of your next turn unless you move, your target [[/act escape dc=31]]{Escapes}, or you attack with the flail, whichever comes first.</p><hr /><p><strong>Activate—Infinite Links</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">3</span> (manipulate)</p>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> You extend the flail's chain, then wrap it across itself and strike two links together. This severs up to a 120-foot loop of usable chain from the flail, which instantly returns to its normal length. If you use Infinite Links again, any previous chain you created with it disappears after 1 round. As with most obviously magical and temporary constructs, the chain can't be sold.</p>",
