    "edition": "remaster",
    "publication": "Pathfinder Impossible Magic",
    "path": "packs/pf2e/equipment/phase-spike.json",
    "description": "<p>The head of this <em>+1 striking astral spear</em> is partially translucent. Thieves and battlefield spellcasters favor it for its ability to pierce magical barriers and temporarily disable enchanted objects. A creature that has Raised its Shield (or similar ability) takes a –1 circumstance penalty to its AC against attacks from a phase spike.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Incorporeal Stride</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">2</span> (concentrate)</p>\n<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> You focus on the head of the spear and channel its properties into your form. You Stride up to your Speed. You can move easily through solid objects and creatures during this movement, but you can't end this movement within a solid object or in a creature's space. You also gain resistance 10 to all damage during this Stride (except force or spirit damage and damage caused by a ghost touch rune); double this resistance against non-magical damage.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "The head of this +1 striking astral spear is partially translucent. Thieves and battlefield spellcasters favor it for its ability to pierce magical barriers and temporarily disable enchanted objects. A creature that has Raised its Shield (or similar ability) takes a –1 circumstance penalty to its AC against attacks from a phase spike. Activate—Incorporeal Stride 2 (concentrate) Frequency once per day Effect You focus on the head of the spear and channel its properties into your form. You Stride up to your Speed. You can move easily through solid objects and creatures during this movement, but you can't end this movement within a solid object or in a creature's space. You also gain resistance 10 to all damage during this Stride (except force or spirit damage and damage caused by a ghost touch rune); double this resistance against non-magical damage.",
