    "description": "<p>The handle, chain, and spiked ball of this <em>+1 striking corrosive flail</em> are all made of iron so rusted that the weapon appears nonfunctional at first glance. On Strikes against a creature that's primarily made of metal, it gains the deadly d10 trait.</p>\n<p><strong>Activate—Rusting Disarm</strong> <span class=\"action-glyph\">R</span></p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> You critically succeed at a @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Disarm] attempt with the flail against a metal weapon</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> Flakes of acid-laden rust are deposited on the disarmed weapon. The weapon takes @Damage[2d6[untyped]] damage, ignoring the weapon's Hardness.</p>",
